@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+---
+id: task-004-let-customers-rent-by-the-hour
+type: task
+title: "Let customers rent by the hour"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and today we have to turn them away. Let customers
+rent by the hour. `addEquipment` now also accepts an `hourlyPrice`, what one hour of rental costs. A
+rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the item's hourly price for each
+hour. An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added optional `hourlyPrice` to the `Equipment` interface in `src/index.ts`.
+- Replaced the old `parseMidnightUtc`/`countWholeDays` pair with a single `validatePeriod` that returns
+  a tagged union: periods of 24h or more are `{ unit: 'daily', days }` and must be midnight-UTC aligned
+  (unchanged rule); periods shorter than 24h are `{ unit: 'hourly', hours }` and must be hour-UTC
+  aligned (new rule).
+- `priceRequest` now branches on that unit: hourly requests are priced at `hours * item.hourlyPrice` and
+  throw when the item has no `hourlyPrice`; daily requests are priced exactly as before, including the
+  long-stay discount (which an hourly request can never reach).
+- `availability` is unaffected beyond accepting hour-aligned sub-day periods as valid, since it only
+  checks whether an item is free, not whether it can be priced for the period.
+- Test-first: added 9 new tests (hourly quote, hourly quote crossing midnight, missing-`hourlyPrice`
+  error for `quote` and `book`, not-on-the-hour start/end errors, hourly `book`, adjacent hourly
+  bookings, hourly `availability`), confirmed they failed against the pre-change code, then implemented
+  until all 29 tests in `test/rental-service.test.ts` pass (`node --test`).
+- Updated 3 pre-existing tests that used a sub-day, hour-aligned-but-not-midnight period to assert "not
+  midnight UTC" throws (`quote`/`book`) or "invalid period" (`availability`): that period is now a
+  legitimate hourly-shaped request, so those tests were changed to a genuinely multi-day non-midnight
+  period (for `quote`/`book`) or a non-hour-aligned period (for `availability`) to keep testing what
+  their names say.
+- Updated `README.md`: documented the hourly-rental rule, that the long-stay discount does not apply to
+  it, and added an `hourlyPrice`/hourly-quote example.
+- Recorded the design choices (how daily vs. hourly is decided, what "on the hour" means, the
+  missing-`hourlyPrice` error, and that `availability` stays price-agnostic) as
+  `dl-003-hourly-rentals-sub-day-periods-priced-by-the-hour-on-the-hour-utc-alignment` (submitted,
+  pending approval).
+
+## Notes
+
+Cancellation and anything beyond pricing/availability of hourly periods remain out of scope, unchanged
+from prior tasks.
